 34S     30SI(A,G),(A,N):RESONANCES    1967WI01,1965MC07,1964VA08ENSDF    202609
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  The ground states of {+30}Si, |a, and {+34}S all have J|p=0+. The      
 34S 2c  resonances in {+34}S populated in {+30}Si+|a have natural parity, and  
 34S 3c  the |g transitions to the {+34}S g.s. are most likely electric, such as
 34S 4c  E1 (1-|)0+) and E2 (2+|)0+).                                           
 34S  c  1967Wi01: {+30}Si(|a,|g) and (|a,n) with 3.25-4.95 MeV |a beams from   
 34S 2c  the 5.5 MeV Van de Graaff accelerator of the Southern Universities     
 34S 3c  Nuclear Institute, South Africa. Targets were 15-40 |mg/cm{+2}, 45%-95%
 34S 4c  enriched {+30}Si targets on tantalum backings. |g rays were detected   
 34S 5c  using NaI(Tl) detectors. Neutrons were detected using a Harwell-form   
 34S 6c  neutron detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q), |g|g(|q), E{-n}, I{-n},   
 34S 7c  and yields. Deduced resonance levels, J, |p, multipolarities, mixing   
 34S 8c  ratios, and resonance strengths.                                       
 34S  c  1965Mc07: {+30}Si(|a,|g) with 3.25-4.25 MeV |a beams. Work was done by 
 34S 2c  the same group as 1967Wi01.                                            
 34S  c  1964Va08: {+30}Si(|a,|g) with 2.1-3.25 MeV |a beams. Work was done by  
 34S 2c  the same group as 1967Wi01 but with the 3 MV Van de Graaff accelerator,
 34S 3c  Utrecht, Netherlands.                                                  
 34S  c  1975DeZS: {+30}Si(|a,|g) with a 2.8-MeV |a beam at Queen's University, 
 34S 2c  Canada. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q). Deduced 4 levels and resonance      
 34S 3c  strengths.                                                             
 34S  c  1979Ku10: {+30}Si(|a,|g) with 4-15 MeV |a beams from the Stanford FN   
 34S 2c  tandem Van de Graaff accelerator. Measured |s(E|g,|q). Deduced E2      
 34S 3c  strength distributions.                                                
 34S  c  All the data are from the paper that reported the level (see the       
 34S 2c  E(level) footnote), except otherwise noted                             
 34S  cG E$Deduced by evaluators from level-energy difference.                  
 34S  cG RI$From 1965Mc07, unless otherwise noted.                              
 34S  cG RI(V)$From 1964Va08.                                                   
 34S  cG RI(W)$From 1967Wi01.                                                   
 34S  cG M,MR$From measured |g(|q) and |g|g(|q) in 1967Wi01, unless otherwise   
 34S 2cG noted.                                                                 
 34S  cL E$From E{-c.m.}+S(|a)({+34}S), where S(|a)({+34}S)=7923.64 {I5}        
 34S 2cL (2021Wa16). E{-c.m.}=E{-|a}(lab)|*m({+30}Si)/[m{-|a}+m({+30}Si)].      
 34S  cL J$From 1967Wi01 by analyzing measured angular distributions, unless    
 34S 2cL otherwise noted.                                                       
 34S  cL E(A),J(A)$From the Adopted Levels.                                     
 34S  cL E(N)$Resonances observed in (|a,n) spectra only (1967Wi01)             
 34S  cL E(G)$Resonances observed in (|a,|g) spectra only (1967Wi01)            
 34S  cL E(H)$1964Va08 states that there is an appreciable |g branch from this  
 34S 2cL resonance to one of the levels higher than 3304 keV.                   
 34S  cL E(Z),J(Z)$From 1975DeZS. 1975DeZS only reports E(level) without        
 34S 2cL E{-|a}(lab).                                                           
 34S  cL S$From 1967Wi01, unless otherwise noted.                               
